#!cgnb 1
%% markdown id=notes
# Pure Boolean branches
Both branches are checked and tracked as dependencies. Changing fallback stales
choose and its caller, even while the true branch is selected. Branch bindings
stay local. Top-level if statements and effectful functions remain unsupported.
%% code id=fallback
fn fallback() -> i64:
    7
%% code id=functions
record Switch:
    active: Bool
    value: i64
fn choose(flag: Bool) -> i64:
    if flag:
        let fallback = 42
        return fallback
    else:
        return fallback()
fn pick(switch: Switch) -> Switch:
    if switch.active:
        return switch
    else:
        return Switch(active: true, value: choose(false))
%% code id=value
let answer = pick(Switch(active: true, value: choose(true)))
answer.value
%% code id=independent
6 * 7
